.TH "NETPLAN\-TRY" "8" "" ""
.SH "نام (NAME)"
\f[CR]netplan\-try\f[R] \- try a configuration, optionally rolling it
back
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan\f[B]\f[R] [\f[I]\-\-debug\f[R]] \f[B]try\f[R]
\f[B]\-h\f[R]|\f[B]\-\-help\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan\f[B]\f[R] [\f[I]\-\-debug\f[R]] \f[B]try\f[R]
[\f[I]\-\-config\-file CONFIG_FILE\f[R]] [\f[I]\-\-timeout TIMEOUT\f[R]]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan try\f[B]\f[R] takes a \f[B]\f[CB]netplan\f[B]\f[R](5)
configuration, applies it, and automatically rolls it back if the user
does not confirm the configuration within a time limit.
.PP
A configuration can be confirmed or rejected interactively or by sending
the SIGUSR1 or SIGINT signals.
.PP
This may be especially useful on remote systems, to prevent an
administrator being permanently locked out of systems in the case of a
network configuration error.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Print basic help.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-debug\f[R]
Print debugging output during the process.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-config\-file\f[R] \f[I]\f[CI]CONFIG_FILE\f[I]\f[R]
In addition to the usual configuration, apply
\f[I]\f[CI]CONFIG_FILE\f[I]\f[R].
It must be a YAML file in the \f[B]\f[CB]netplan\f[B]\f[R](5) format.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-timeout\f[R] \f[I]\f[CI]TIMEOUT\f[I]\f[R]
Wait for \f[I]\f[CI]TIMEOUT\f[I]\f[R] seconds before reverting.
Defaults to 120 seconds.
Note that some network configurations (such as STP) may take over a
minute to settle.
.SH KNOWN ISSUES
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan try\f[B]\f[R] uses similar procedures to
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan apply\f[B]\f[R], so some of the same caveats apply
around virtual devices.
.PP
There are also some known bugs: if \f[B]\f[CB]netplan try\f[B]\f[R]
times out or is cancelled, make sure to verify if the network
configuration has in fact been reverted.
.PP
As with \f[B]\f[CB]netplan apply\f[B]\f[R], a reboot should fix any
issues.
However, be sure to verify that the configuration on disk is in the
state you expect before rebooting!
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan\f[B]\f[R](5),
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan\-generate\f[B]\f[R](8),
\f[B]\f[CB]netplan\-apply\f[B]\f[R](8)
